# Real orchestrated hands-off loop — packaged + two honest phase end-tests

The decompose → scoped-dispatch → independent-judge → frozen-verify
loop was proven LIVES at unit scale by the Tier-0 probe. This
amendment does NOT re-prove that (AC.FOUND.0) — it packages the
proven mechanism as a primary-persona-invocable capability and runs
the two honest end-tests for the two unknowns the probe left open:
(A) does a packaged, reusable mechanism orchestrate as cleanly as a
person hand-driving did; (B) can a non-technical user's fuzzy
plain-language intent be turned into a faithful machine-checkable
"done" without the user writing a spec.

Surface added:
  - framework/tools/handsoff-loop/ — the executable orchestration
    package: orchestrator (decompose→dispatch real claude -p
    sub-agents→independent tool-executing judge, composing the
    probe-proven mechanism, NOT re-proving it), intake leg
    (fuzzy intent → bounded elicit-the-minimum → plain-language
    acceptance + one approval → machine-checkable + faithfulness
    check), frozen-unseen independent + anti-overfit verifier, and
    the /goal-under-`-p` drive/stop wiring (loam's tool-executing
    check decides; /goal drives).
  - plugins/loam-skills/skills/handsoff-loop/SKILL.md — the
    persona-invocable packaging (auto-surfaces, one capability,
    delegates to the tools package).
  - framework/hands-off-lifecycle/tests/test_AC_HL_*.py — one file
    per AC; deterministic structural ACs in the seal sweep; the two
    phase end-tests real-claude-driven with captured verdict tables.

Phase A and Phase B each produced a definite, evidence-backed
per-dimension verdict table. A definite NEGATIVE on either phase is
a valid plan-success outcome — reported straight, never retried to
green, never softened. Tier C attempted iff both phases positive,
else gated (not failed). Cost measured via --output-format json
against the $2-8 / <=20 min band.

Composes the verified-real /goal built-in (binary 2.1.143) for the
drive/stop leg ONLY; loam's independent tool-executing check decides
via its surfaced exit code — /goal's Haiku transcript-only evaluator
keys off that surfaced verdict, never sub-agent prose. No
re-implementation of turn-after-turn drive; /goal is never the
artefact judge (Lens-1).

Single-component fence: framework/workspace-bootstrap/. NOT merged
to main, NOT pushed, NOT published, NOT tagged — sealed-local-on-
branch is the deliverable; origin/main unchanged. NO Anthropic API
key — real claude binary, default Sonnet.
